From 6278f2f1e29abf4ef66e9011cd3824a2aee434ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:51:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] USB: cdc-wdm: Clear the stale response state on resume

wdm_int_callback() sets WDM_RESPONDING and raises resp_count before it
checks whether it may submit the response URB. If the notification
arrives while WDM_SUSPENDING is set, no URB is submitted, rv stays 0,
and the cleanup that would clear WDM_RESPONDING is skipped.

wdm_resume() clears only WDM_SUSPENDING, so the pair survives the
resume. Every later notification then finds the device already
"responding" and never issues GET_ENCAPSULATED_RESPONSE, leaving the
character device open and permanently silent - no error anywhere. Only
the last close clears it, which is why reopening from another process
does not help while anything still holds the device.

Seen on a PinePhone with a Quectel EG25-G: after every system resume,
QMI requests on /dev/cdc-wdm0 time out with no error, for existing
client IDs, for a fresh QMI_CTL client ID allocation, and for a newly
opened /dev/cdc-wdm0 alike, while the modem answers AT commands on its
other interfaces normally. Closing every opener and reopening restores
it, and so does unbinding the driver.

Clear the stale response state on resume, before resubmitting the
interrupt URB so a notification cannot race in and latch it again. The
outstanding response is dropped rather than fetched: it no longer
exists after the bus reset a system resume brings, and the next
notification re-arms the endpoint normally.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/class/cdc-wdm.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/class/cdc-wdm.c b/drivers/usb/class/cdc-wdm.c
index 7556c0dac908..09764cbd0bcd 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/class/cdc-wdm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/class/cdc-wdm.c
@@ -1312,6 +1312,29 @@ static int wdm_resume(struct usb_interface *intf)
 	dev_dbg(&desc->intf->dev, "wdm%d_resume\n", intf->minor);
 
 	clear_bit(WDM_SUSPENDING, &desc->flags);
+
+	/*
+	 * A RESPONSE_AVAILABLE notification arriving while WDM_SUSPENDING was
+	 * set leaves WDM_RESPONDING set and resp_count raised by
+	 * wdm_int_callback(), without the response URB ever being submitted.
+	 * Nothing clears that pair until the last close, so every later
+	 * notification finds the device already "responding" and no
+	 * GET_ENCAPSULATED_RESPONSE is ever issued again: the character device
+	 * stays open, and silent, for good.
+	 *
+	 * Drop the stale response instead. It cannot be fetched anyway after
+	 * the bus reset that a system resume brings, and the next notification
+	 * then re-arms the endpoint normally. Do it before resubmitting the
+	 * interrupt URB, or a notification can race in and latch again.
+	 *
+	 * Nothing is in flight here: wdm_suspend() poisoned the URBs and
+	 * cancelled the work.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_irq(&desc->iuspin);
+	desc->resp_count = 0;
+	clear_bit(WDM_RESPONDING, &desc->flags);
+	spin_unlock_irq(&desc->iuspin);
+
 	rv = recover_from_urb_loss(desc);
 
 	return rv;
-- 
